From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:37:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 138/151] Find: Replace all line by line is one undo step

Replace all for a query searched line by line replaced one match per
edit, so undoing it took one Ctrl+Z per match. It now finds every
non-empty match first and replaces them in one change, like the joined
path, with the cursor after the last replacement. Empty matches are
skipped, as the match count and the joined path skip them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

